            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/topology.cpp",
                    "line": 110,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "I'm not sure why clang-tidy isn't complaining about an unchecked optional access.  Maybe because it isn't possible as stated below?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/topology.cpp",
                    "line": 110,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "It did complain, just saw there was a Verified -1.\n\nI did not run CI locally due to the number of patches. Fixed it in latest revision."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/topology.cpp",
                    "line": 125,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "Why returning an optional? Shouldn't a reverse association always exist?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/topology.cpp",
                    "line": 125,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Fixed it in a later patch. As of this patch the associations are still modeled on strings so from a single functions perspective we do not know if our input string will be part of the map.\n\nSo this patch is more of a transition step to avoid explicitly listing both the forward and reverse association.\n\nLater the whole function will go away again as it will not be needed anymore."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/topology.cpp",
                    "line": 139,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "'Reverse' has a specific meaning in assocations https://github.com/openbmc/docs/blob/master/architecture/object-mapper.md#associations.  While you do just use it to get the reverse one, I see the function can return either.  Maybe 'getOpposite'?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/entity_manager/topology.cpp",
                    "line": 139,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes, it could be misleading. My interpretation was that the order does not matter,\nbut i renamed as `getOppositeAssoc` to avoid any confusions."
                }
            ],
